whether in our country, whether in Europe, you see it in many different places. That, and their behavior is reminiscent of leaders in the past who went on to do very terrible things, both to their own people and to other countries, inhabitants of other countries. So it's a balance. And speaking about today's situation and comparing it to the 1930s, I'm start with the 1930s. I grew up, you know, amongst many refugees from Hitler, I grew up on the Upper West Side of Manhattan. I never saw in my lifetime, more loyal citizens to the United States, people whose devotion to the United States of America was overwhelming.
